+# Feature Specification: Hourly rental
+
+**Created**: 2026-11-11 | **Status**: Implemented
+
+## User Scenarios & Testing
+
+### User Story 1 - Rent a board for an afternoon (P1)
+`addEquipment` accepts an optional `hourlyPrice` (non-negative integer cents per hour). A rental shorter than a day whose start and end are on the hour costs hours × hourlyPrice.
+**Acceptance**:
+1. Given hourlyPrice 600, a 09:00–13:00 rental quotes and books at 2400.
+2. Given an item without hourlyPrice, a sub-day rental is rejected.
+3. Sub-day rentals not on the hour are rejected; no long-stay discount applies.
+
+## Requirements
+- **FR-001**: duration < 24h: total = hours × hourlyPrice; start/end must be on the hour.
+- **FR-002**: duration >= 24h: unchanged; start/end must be midnight UTC.
+- **FR-003**: Hourly bookings block overlapping bookings of the same item.
+- **FR-004**: `availability` still takes midnight-to-midnight periods (unchanged), but sees hourly bookings.
+
+## Assumptions
+- Constitution is an unfilled template; no extra rules apply.
+- A sub-day rental may cross midnight.
